// The family's own server on tvOS:
// - users: sign-in tiles for accounts that the server hides from its public user list, shown only on that server.
// - addresses: tried by Automatic on the add-server screen, such as the server's Tailscale address,
//   so an Apple TV running Tailscale finds the server away from home.
// Copy this file to FamilyServer.xcconfig, which is gitignored, and replace the value.
// Builds without that file show the server's public users only, and Automatic finds servers on the local network only.
//
// FAMILY_SERVER is URL-safe base64 of JSON with the server's ID (GET /System/Info/Public), its users,
// whose fields are named as the Jellyfin API returns them, and its addresses. Both lists are optional.
// This example decodes to:
//   {"serverID":"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef","users":[{"Id":"11111111111111111111111111111111","Name":"Avery"},{"Id":"22222222222222222222222222222222","Name":"Quinn"}],"addresses":["http://media-server.tail0000.ts.net:8096"]}
// Encode with: base64 -i server.json | tr -d '\n' | tr '+/' '-_'
// URL-safe because xcconfig reads "//" as the start of a comment.

FAMILY_SERVER = 
